<template compat="shopify">
{%- comment -%}
  Materia Themes. target and rel for one link, only when the creator asked
  for that link to open in a new tab:
  - new_tab / legacy_new_tab: the link's own toggle in a block or section
    (legacy_new_tab is the old id, read when new_tab is not set);
  - link: a menu link. Navigation stores its "Open in a new tab" as #_blank on
    the link's address; a target, new_tab, open_in_new_tab, newTab or
    open_new_tab property on the link is read too.
  A link nobody flagged never gets a target, same site or not. Print the
  address with | remove: '#_blank' so the marker never reaches the href.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if new_tab == nil
    assign new_tab = legacy_new_tab
  endif
  assign open_new = false
  if new_tab == true
    assign open_new = true
  endif
  if url contains '#_blank'
    assign open_new = true
  endif
  if link != blank
    if link.target == '_blank' or link.new_tab == true or link.open_in_new_tab == true or link.newTab == true or link.open_new_tab == true
      assign open_new = true
    endif
    if link.url contains '#_blank'
      assign open_new = true
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if open_new -%}target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"{%- endif -%}
</template>
